WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.288
Reptiles are found on all the continents of the world except Antarctica.
除南极洲外，世界各地都有爬行动物。

2
00:00:06.288 --> 00:00:20.280
There are four main types of reptiles: lizards and snakes, crocodiles and alligators, turtles and tortoises, and tuatara, which are only found in New Zealand.
爬行动物主要有四类：蜥蜴和蛇、鳄鱼和短吻鳄、海龟和陆龟，以及仅生活在新西兰的喙头蜥。

3
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.744
Each reptile has its own distinct features.
每种爬行动物都有自己独特的特征。

4
00:00:24.744 --> 00:00:29.352
Snakes are reptiles which do not have limbs.
蛇是没有四肢的爬行动物。

5
00:00:29.352 --> 00:00:35.136
The shell of a tortoise is part of its skeleton on the outside of its body.
陆龟的壳是长在体外的骨骼的一部分。

6
00:00:35.136 --> 00:00:38.472
It is called an exoskeleton.
这叫做外骨骼。

7
00:00:38.472 --> 00:00:43.152
A veiled chameleon has its own distinct features.
高冠变色龙也有自己独特的特征。

8
00:00:43.152 --> 00:00:48.672
Some species of lizard drop their tails to escape predators.
有些蜥蜴会断尾逃跑，躲避捕食者。

9
00:00:48.672 --> 00:00:56.472
Some reptiles live on land, while others like crocodiles spend much of their time in the water.
有些生活在陆地，有些如鳄鱼大部分时间在水里。

10
00:00:56.472 --> 00:01:01.032
All reptiles have lungs and need air to breathe.
所有爬行动物都有肺，需要空气才能呼吸。

11
00:01:01.032 --> 00:01:07.704
Reptiles are cold-blooded, which means they cannot control their body temperature.
爬行动物是冷血动物，不能自己调节体温。

12
00:01:07.704 --> 00:01:14.832
Most reptiles lay eggs, but some reptiles such as skinks give birth to live young.
大多数产卵，但有些石龙子直接生下幼崽。

13
00:01:14.832 --> 00:01:19.320
Most reptiles are carnivores and eat meat.
大多数爬行动物是食肉动物。

14
00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.072
Turtles and tortoises are mostly herbivores.
海龟和陆龟大多是食草动物。
